  "id": "parlodel",
  "term": "Parlodel",
  "definition": "Parlodel is bromocriptine mesylate, a drug form of a semisynthetic ergot compound that acts mainly by stimulating dopamine D2 receptors in the central nervous system and pituitary gland. Its effects include reducing certain abnormal movement-related signaling and lowering prolactin release, which can suppress lactation.",
